# Trivy ignore list for CI image/dependency scans (see .github/workflows/ci.yaml).
#
# Every entry here is a documented, reviewed exception — not a way to
# silence the scanner. Each CVE ID must have a comment explaining why it
# doesn't apply to how this application actually runs. Remove an entry as
# soon as a fixed base image is available, or if the container's runtime
# model changes in a way that makes the CVE relevant again.

# --- frontend (nginx:1.31-alpine) ---
# util-linux/libuuid mount(8)/nsenter privilege-escalation and TOCTOU
# CVEs. All require CAP_SYS_ADMIN and the ability to invoke privileged
# mount/nsenter operations. This container runs `nginx` as the
# unprivileged `nginx` user (USER nginx in frontend/Dockerfile), serves
# only static files, and never calls mount/nsenter. In Kubernetes the
# pod additionally runs under the PodSecurityStandards "restricted"
# profile (no added capabilities, non-root). No fixed version exists yet
# in Alpine's current stable release as of the image used.
CVE-2026-53612
CVE-2026-53613
CVE-2026-53614
CVE-2026-76642
CVE-2026-78408
CVE-2026-78409
CVE-2026-78410
